---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Team Tasks Manager — team coordination, inside Discord">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Team Tasks Manager</p>
    <h1>Coordinate your team where it already talks.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Stop juggling Discord and a pile of external task tools. <strong>Team Tasks Manager</strong> brings shared checklists, reminders and roles right into your server &mdash; so attention stays in one place.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="#">Add to Discord</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="/docs/">Read the docs &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block wrap">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">The problem</p>
    <h2>Coordination shouldn't cost you your focus.</h2>
    <div class="split-cols">
      <div class="panel pain">
        <h3>Without TTM</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><span class="tick">&mdash;</span><span>Tasks live in a <b>separate tool</b> (boards, spreadsheets, another app) while the team talks on Discord.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&mdash;</span><span>Every update means <b>switching context</b>, copying links, re-explaining status.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&mdash;</span><span>Deadlines slip because <b>nobody owns the reminder</b>.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&mdash;</span><span>Attention is <b>scattered</b> across windows and no one has the full picture.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel gain">
        <h3>With TTM</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><span class="tick">+</span><span>Shared, trackable checklists <b>inside the channel</b> where work is discussed.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">+</span><span>Assign tasks to <b>people or roles</b>, and tag who to notify on completion.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">+</span><span>Automatic <b>reminders</b> carry the burden of remembering for you.</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">+</span><span>One source of truth &mdash; the whole team sees the same board, in real time.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block wrap">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Why we built it</p>
    <h2>The tools weren't bad. They were somewhere else.</h2>
    <p class="big">We built TTM for ourselves first. As the work grew, every external tool we tried to coordinate the team with failed for the same reason: it lived <strong>outside Discord</strong>. Each update meant leaving the conversation and coming back, so none of them ever became part of the routine &mdash; and carrying information across, in both directions, quietly turned into a job of its own.</p>
    <p class="big" style="margin-top:1.2rem">So we're firm about one thing: <strong>a tool is only effective if it's easy to use and easy to configure</strong>, and it only stays easy if it never asks you to leave the place where you already are. That's why <strong>you will never find an external dashboard here</strong>. Everything TTM does &mdash; and everything you configure &mdash; happens inside Discord, with buttons, menus and modals.</p>
    <div class="callout" style="max-width:60ch; margin-top:1.4rem"><div class="callout-t">Where does this site fit, then?</div>It's documentation, not a control panel. The same goes for the <a href="https://timezones.bitsplitters.app">time zone picker</a> the bot links to: a helper page, one job, no account. Neither one holds your data or your settings &mdash; there is nothing to log into, because there is nothing there that belongs to you.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="block wrap">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">What you get</p>
    <h2>Everything runs on Discord's own interface.</h2>
    <p class="big">Almost no slash commands to memorize: every feature is a button with a familiar icon, designed to take the fewest clicks possible.</p>
    <div class="grid3">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head"><img class="ic" src="/icons/task_list.png" alt="" /><h3>Shared lists</h3></div>
        <p>Create a checklist from plain text. Tasks, subtasks and task groups are recognized automatically from line breaks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head"><img class="ic" src="/icons/owner.png" alt="" /><h3>Owners &amp; tags</h3></div>
        <p>Give each task an owner and tag the people or roles to notify &mdash; right on the task, not in a side conversation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head"><img class="ic" src="/icons/alertW.png" alt="" /><h3>Reminders</h3></div>
        <p>Attach a reminder with start date, interval, repetitions and time zone. TTM remembers so you don't have to.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="block wrap">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Try it</p>
    <h2>This is what a list looks like in your server.</h2>
    <p class="big">A message the bot keeps up to date, with a dropdown underneath to tick tasks off. Nothing to learn: it's Discord's own interface, so it already behaves the way you expect.</p>

    <!-- Mock della lista come la rende il bot: intestazione del messaggio, titolo H2, righe
         numerate con checkbox, e sotto la select per spuntare i task. L'animazione mostra il
         gesto piu' frequente — apri la select, scegli un task, la riga si spunta — perche' e'
         quello che rende il bot familiare prima ancora di invitarlo. -->
    <div class="dc-demo">
      <div class="dc-msg">
        <img class="dc-avatar" src="/icons/TTM-Official.png" alt="" />
        <div class="dc-body">
          <div class="dc-head">
            <span class="dc-name">Team Tasks Manager</span>
            <span class="dc-app">APP</span>
            <span class="dc-time">Today at 18:04</span>
          </div>

          <div class="dc-title">Roster &amp; scrims &mdash; week 12</div>
          <ul class="dc-tasks">
            <li data-task="1" class="dc-done">
              <span class="dc-n">1</span>
              <span class="dc-cb">
                <img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" />
                <img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" />
              </span>
              <span class="dc-txt">Confirm the five-man roster for Saturday's scrim block</span>
            </li>
            <li data-task="2" class="dc-flip">
              <span class="dc-n">2</span>
              <span class="dc-cb">
                <img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" />
                <img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" />
              </span>
              <span class="dc-txt">Lock the scrim block vs. Nova Collective</span>
            </li>
            <li data-task="2.1" data-parent="2" class="dc-sub">
              <span class="dc-n">2.1</span>
              <span class="dc-cb">
                <img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" />
                <img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" />
              </span>
              <span class="dc-txt">Clip the three teamfights for the review</span>
            </li>
            <li data-task="3">
              <span class="dc-n">3</span>
              <span class="dc-cb">
                <img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" />
                <img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" />
              </span>
              <span class="dc-txt">VOD review: mid rotations, game 3 <span class="dc-pill">@coach</span></span>
              <span class="dc-meta"><img src="/icons/alertW.png" alt="" />in 2 days at 20:30 &middot; repeats weekly</span>
            </li>
            <li data-task="4" class="dc-done">
              <span class="dc-n">4</span>
              <span class="dc-cb">
                <img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" />
                <img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" />
              </span>
              <span class="dc-txt">Submit the tournament registration</span>
            </li>
            <li data-task="5">
              <span class="dc-n">5</span>
              <span class="dc-cb">
                <img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" />
                <img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" />
              </span>
              <span class="dc-txt">Publish the match-day graphic <span class="dc-pill">@social</span></span>
              <span class="dc-meta"><img src="/icons/wb.png" alt="" />webhook: post-to-x</span>
            </li>
            <li data-task="6">
              <span class="dc-n">6</span>
              <span class="dc-cb">
                <img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" />
                <img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" />
              </span>
              <span class="dc-txt">Chase the two missing player contracts</span>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="dc-select">
            <button type="button" class="dc-select-btn" id="dc-trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="dc-menu">
              <span class="dc-select-lab">Check or uncheck tasks</span>
              <span class="dc-caret">&#9662;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="dc-select-menu" id="dc-menu" role="group" aria-label="Check or uncheck tasks">
              <button type="button" class="dc-opt" data-for="1" aria-pressed="true"><span class="dc-optcb"><img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" /><img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" /></span>1 &middot; Confirm the five-man roster</button>
              <button type="button" class="dc-opt dc-opt-pick" data-for="2" aria-pressed="false"><span class="dc-optcb"><img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" /><img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" /></span>2 &middot; Lock the scrim block vs. Nova Collective</button>
              <button type="button" class="dc-opt" data-for="2.1" aria-pressed="false"><span class="dc-optcb"><img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" /><img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" /></span>2.1 &middot; Clip the three teamfights</button>
              <button type="button" class="dc-opt" data-for="3" aria-pressed="false"><span class="dc-optcb"><img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" /><img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" /></span>3 &middot; VOD review: mid rotations</button>
              <button type="button" class="dc-opt" data-for="4" aria-pressed="true"><span class="dc-optcb"><img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" /><img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" /></span>4 &middot; Submit the tournament registration</button>
              <button type="button" class="dc-opt" data-for="5" aria-pressed="false"><span class="dc-optcb"><img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" /><img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" /></span>5 &middot; Publish the match-day graphic</button>
              <button type="button" class="dc-opt" data-for="6" aria-pressed="false"><span class="dc-optcb"><img class="dc-cb-off" src="/icons/checkbox_empty.png" alt="" /><img class="dc-cb-on" src="/icons/checkbox_marked.png" alt="" /></span>6 &middot; Chase the two missing contracts</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="dc-hint" id="dc-hint">Open the selector and tick a task &mdash; it works exactly like this in Discord. Group <strong>2</strong> and its subtask move together.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="big" style="margin-top:2.5rem">And these are the buttons that sit under it &mdash; no labels, on purpose. Trust your intuition, then click to confirm what each one does.</p>
    <div class="board-teaser">
      <div class="board-lab">Row 1 &mdash; acts on the whole list</div>
      <div class="board-row">
        <button class="dbtn" data-name="Clone list" data-desc="Clone the list into other channels of the server. A dropdown lets you pick the destination channel, and you can choose whether to keep task selections and reminders."><img src="/icons/clone.png" alt="Clone list" /></button>
        <button class="dbtn" data-name="Download" data-desc="Download a text file with the list, ready to copy and paste into other lists — even on other servers."><img src="/icons/download.png" alt="Download" /></button>
        <button class="dbtn" data-name="Bulk update" data-desc="Edit the title and the whole list at once — the fastest way to change two or more tasks together."><img src="/icons/edit.png" alt="Bulk update" /></button>
        <button class="dbtn" data-name="Clean list" data-desc="Remove all selected tasks from the list and recalculate the remaining positions automatically."><img src="/icons/clean.png" alt="Clean list" /></button>
        <button class="dbtn" data-name="More" data-desc="Opens the panel with everything you rarely need: the in-Discord guide describing every button, and the deletion of the list — which takes its reminders with it."><img src="/icons/other.png" alt="More" /></button>
      </div>
      <div class="board-lab">Row 2 &mdash; acts on a single task &middot; click to cycle grey &rarr; blue (edit) &rarr; red (delete)</div>
      <div class="board-row">
        <button class="dbtn task-btn" data-name="Content" data-edit="Change the task text." data-delete="Delete the task."><img src="/icons/task.png" alt="Content" /></button>
        <button class="dbtn task-btn" data-name="Owner" data-edit="Set or change the task owner." data-delete="Remove the owner."><img src="/icons/owner.png" alt="Owner" /></button>
        <button class="dbtn task-btn" data-name="Tag" data-edit="Add a user or role to notify at the end of the task." data-delete="Remove every tag on the task."><img src="/icons/tag.png" alt="Tag" /></button>
        <button class="dbtn task-btn" data-name="Reminder" data-edit="Add or edit a reminder (start date, interval, repetitions, time zone)." data-delete="Remove the reminder."><img src="/icons/alertW.png" alt="Reminder" /></button>
        <button class="dbtn task-btn" data-name="Webhook" data-edit="Associate a webhook, so completing or reopening the task fires an HTTP call." data-delete="Remove the webhook association from the task."><img src="/icons/api.png" alt="Webhook" /></button>
      </div>
      <div class="board-info" id="board-info">Click any button above. <strong>Row 1</strong> acts on the whole list; <strong>Row 2</strong> buttons cycle through three states &mdash; click one to walk through them.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block wrap">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Go deeper</p>
    <h2>Ready to set it up?</h2>
    <p class="big">The documentation walks you through inviting the bot, creating your first list, mastering the panel, configuring the app and connecting webhooks.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
      <a class="btn" href="/docs/getting-started/">Get started &rarr;</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="/docs/">Browse all docs</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    /* ── Il mock della lista: interattivo come la pulsantiera ──────────────────────────────────
       Riproduce il "check selector" descritto in /docs/the-task-list/: spunta e despunta i task,
       e un gruppo trascina i suoi sottotask. La cascata e' nei DUE sensi, come nel bot: spuntare
       il gruppo spunta i figli, e quando TUTTI i figli sono spuntati il gruppo si spunta da se'.
       Riprodurre solo il primo senso avrebbe insegnato mezza verita'. */
    const demo = document.querySelector(".dc-demo");
    if (demo) {
      const sel = demo.querySelector(".dc-select");
      const trigger = demo.querySelector(".dc-select-btn");
      const opzioni = Array.from(demo.querySelectorAll(".dc-opt"));
      const righe = Array.from(demo.querySelectorAll(".dc-tasks li"));
      const hint = document.getElementById("dc-hint");

      const riga = (id) => righe.find((r) => r.dataset.task === id);
      const opzione = (id) => opzioni.find((o) => o.dataset.for === id);
      const spuntato = (id) => { const r = riga(id); return !!r && r.classList.contains("dc-done"); };

      // Al primo tocco l'animazione dimostrativa si ferma: da quel momento comanda la persona, e
      // vedere la riga 2 spuntarsi da sola mentre ci si sta giocando sarebbe solo confusione.
      const fermaAnimazione = () => demo.classList.add("dc-live");

      const imposta = (id, valore) => {
        const r = riga(id);
        if (!r) return;
        r.classList.toggle("dc-done", valore);
        const o = opzione(id);
        if (o) o.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(valore));
      };

      const applica = (id) => {
        const valore = !spuntato(id);
        imposta(id, valore);

        // giu': il gruppo trascina i figli
        righe.filter((r) => r.dataset.parent === id).forEach((r) => imposta(r.dataset.task, valore));

        // su': se tutti i figli sono spuntati il genitore lo diventa, e basta un figlio aperto
        // perche' il genitore torni aperto
        const r = riga(id);
        const padre = r && r.dataset.parent;
        if (padre) {
          const figli = righe.filter((x) => x.dataset.parent === padre);
          imposta(padre, figli.every((x) => x.classList.contains("dc-done")));
        }
      };

      const apriChiudi = (aperto) => {
        sel.classList.toggle("open", aperto);
        trigger.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(aperto));
      };

      trigger.addEventListener("click", () => {
        fermaAnimazione();
        apriChiudi(!sel.classList.contains("open"));
      });

      opzioni.forEach((o) => o.addEventListener("click", () => {
        fermaAnimazione();
        applica(o.dataset.for);
        // Il menu NON si chiude: la select del bot e' multipla, e chiuderla a ogni scelta
        // costringerebbe a riaprirla per il task successivo.
        if (hint) hint.textContent = "That's it — the message updates in place, and the selector stays open so you can tick more than one.";
      }));

      document.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
        if (sel.classList.contains("open") && !sel.contains(e.target)) apriChiudi(false);
      });
      document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
        if (e.key === "Escape" && sel.classList.contains("open")) { apriChiudi(false); trigger.focus(); }
      });
    }

    const info = document.getElementById("board-info");
    document.querySelectorAll(".board-row .dbtn:not(.task-btn)").forEach((b) => {
      b.addEventListener("click", () => {
        info.innerHTML = "<strong>" + b.dataset.name + "</strong><br>" + b.dataset.desc;
      });
    });
    const taskBtns = document.querySelectorAll(".task-btn");
    taskBtns.forEach((b) => {
      b.dataset.state = "0";
      b.addEventListener("click", () => {
        // Only one task button can be active at a time: reset the others to grey
        taskBtns.forEach((o) => { if (o !== b) { o.dataset.state = "0"; o.classList.remove("is-edit", "is-delete"); } });
        const state = (parseInt(b.dataset.state, 10) + 1) % 3;
        b.dataset.state = String(state);
        b.classList.toggle("is-edit", state === 1);
        b.classList.toggle("is-delete", state === 2);
        const name = b.dataset.name;
        if (state === 1) info.innerHTML = "<strong>" + name + " &mdash; edit</strong><br>" + b.dataset.edit;
        else if (state === 2) info.innerHTML = "<strong>" + name + " &mdash; delete</strong><br>" + b.dataset.delete;
        else info.innerHTML = "<strong>" + name + " &mdash; off</strong><br>Inactive. While every task button is grey, the check selector toggles tasks.";
      });
    });
  </script>
</Base>
